# What this corpus draws no page for. One entry per line -- a basename
# for a program that produces no page at all, a basename and " pN" for
# one page of a program that produces others -- each with the reason it
# draws nothing.
#
# A run compares the pages both engines drew, so anything that draws
# none is outside the comparison and the run answers nothing about it.
# Saying so here in advance is what keeps that from passing for a
# result: the count of programs a corpus evaluated is honest and says
# only that they were reached, so a run in which every program failed
# reports exactly what a run in which every one rendered reports. An
# absence nobody declared fails the corpus for that reason. So does a
# declared absence that turns out to have rendered -- the entry's reason
# has lapsed, and the line is left telling its next reader something
# untrue.
